<title>USA: Elkem raises chromium metal prices.</title>
<headline>Elkem raises chromium metal prices.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-05-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>Elkem Metals, the U.S. subsidiary of Norway's Elkem A/S, said it has raised its chromium metals prices, effective May 28, by 45 cents per pound for vacuum grade products, and 35 cents per pound for regular grade and powder products.</p>
<p>The new price for regular vacuum grade chromium is $5.75 per pound, FOB Marietta, Ohio for truckload quantities.</p>
<p>((New York Commodity Desk 212-859-1646))</p>
